  "question": {
    "text": "An object is placed in a medium of refractive index <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn></math>. An electromagnetic wave of intensity <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>8</mn></msup><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">W</mi><mo> </mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math> falls normally on the object and it is absorbed completely. The radiation pressure on the object would be (speed of light in free space <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>8</mn></msup><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo> </mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> ):"
  },
